    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as the anchor of the lineup with an elite score of 76.69. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Pallante, and his projected efficiency is significantly buoyed by a slow SP delivery, which elevates his stolen base potential to a maximum 100% viability factor\u2014a critical component for Ghost Ride the WHIP given our scarcity-focused strategy. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (69.99) and **Brice Turang** (70.18) provide high-floor production. **Jose Caballero** in particular is a primary beneficiary of a dynamic platoon edge (+13%) and the same favorable base-stealing environment, making the bottom of the order highly weaponized against the opposition.\n\nWhile we remain aggressive on the basepaths, we are exercising caution with **James Wood** (51.16). Despite his elite 0.402 xwOBA, he faces a difficult matchup against an elite defensive catcher with a 1.88s pop time, which suppresses his aggressive SB profile by 1%. Our most difficult sit-start decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who scored a respectable 59.90. While his park factors (+14%) and platoon advantage (+7%) made a compelling case, he narrowly missed the starting cut as we prioritize the high-upside ceiling of **Corbin Carroll** and the lineup security of **Brice Turang**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki**, who remains benched due to a rainout/postponement, and monitoring the status of **Trevor Story**, who continues to occupy an IL slot. We have no active exposure to **Josh Naylor**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, or **Henry Bolte** for this specific rotation.",
